course: dictionary
lesson: 8257
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word rich is a good example. To find out which meaning the writer means, read the words around it, which are its context. «The Chinese kept the method of making silk secret for centuries, so rich people from Rome to Persia paid a fortune for it.» Here rich people means people with a lot of money.
explain: Now read this: «The Blue Nile brings the rich silt that once flooded Egypt every year.» Silt is the soft mud that washes down a river. Rich silt is good for growing plants, so the clue is in the word that comes after rich. Always ask: what does rich mean in this sentence and nowhere else?
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. If you swap in «the lots of money silt», it does not make sense, so that is not the meaning here. Finding the right meaning is a detective job, and the clues are always in the text.
fact: Rich can mean having a lot of money or valuable things.
fact: Rich food has a lot of butter, cream, sugar or fat, and it fills you up quickly.
fact: «Rich in» means containing a lot of something good, such as «rich in vitamins».
fact: Rich soil is good for growing plants, and a rich colour or sound is deep and strong.
fact: Rich can change its form: richer and richest compare how much money or good things someone has.
exercise: «The Chinese kept silk-making secret, so rich people from Rome to Persia paid a fortune for it.» What does rich mean here? | Good for growing plants | *Having a lot of money | Full of butter and cream | A deep, strong sound
exercise: «The Blue Nile brings the rich silt that once flooded Egypt every year.» What does rich mean in this sentence? | Lots of gold and jewels | Deep and loud | *Good for growing plants | Fatty and filling for dinner
exercise: Mum says, «This chocolate cake is very rich, so one small slice is enough.» What does rich mean? | Having lots of money | A deep, strong colour | *Full of butter, cream and sugar, so it fills you up | Good for growing plants
test: Which sentence uses rich to mean rich in vitamins? | A rich colour filled the sky | *Oranges are rich in vitamin C | A rich person bought a big house | The rich soil grew tall corn
test: Ella reads, «The rich and the poor both came to the park.» What does the rich mean here? | *The people who have a lot of money | The people who cook the best food | The people who sing the loudest | The people who grow plants
exam: Jayden reads, «Her voice was rich and deep, like a cello.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | *Deep and strong, because rich describes a sound and a cello sounds deep | Full of butter, because a cello is made of wood | Having lots of money, because a cello costs a fortune | Good for growing plants, because a cello grows in soil
